===Levels 35+: Cannonballs===
[[Steel cannonball]]s can be made after the completion of the [[Dwarf Cannon]] quest and they can be useful for certain [[Ironman Guide/Slayer|Slayer]] scenarios. However, due to their slow forging speed of 4 cannonballs every 4.8 seconds with the regular [[ammo mould]], it is recommended to purchase the [[double ammo mould]] from [[Giants' Foundry]] to double the production rate to 8 cannonballs every 4.8 seconds. Additionally, players can make use of the [[Ancient Furnace]] to double the production rate to 4 cannonballs every 2.4 seconds with the regular [[ammo mould]] or 8 cannonballs every 2.4 seconds with the [[Double ammo mould]].

Regular [[ammo mould]] at the [[Edgeville Furnace]]:
*2,160 cannonballs per hour
*13,824 Smithing experience per hour

[[Double ammo mould]] at the [[Edgeville Furnace]]:
*4,320 cannonballs per hour
*27,648 Smithing experience per hour
[[Coal]] and [[iron ore]] can be quickly bought from [[Ordan]] at the Blast Furnace and smelt into [[steel bars]] for cannonballs. To get from 40 to 70 Ranged while primarily using a [[Dwarf multicannon|cannon]] for [[Pay-to-play Ranged training|Ranged training]], you'll need about 35,000 cannonballs, requiring 8,750 steel bars. 

If you need a large quantity of iron and coal ores for smithing [[steel bars]] into cannonballs, it's more efficient to spend time earning money to buy ores from [[Ordan]] instead of directly mining them. If you can earn 200,000 coins per hour from [[Thieving]] or the [[Agility Pyramid]], you can purchase around 4,000 iron ore or 1,400 coal from Ordan and bank at the nearby chest. Assuming you would normally mine and bank 1,000 ores an hour, this represents a significant increase in the number of ores you would be able to obtain.

===Levels 75/90-99: Making Hastae (Requires 99 fishing)===

===== Background =====
{{Inventory|align=right
|Achievement diary cape|Yew logs|Yew logs|Yew logs
|Fishing cape|Yew logs|Yew logs|Yew logs
|Yew logs|Yew logs|Yew logs|Yew logs
|Yew logs|Yew logs|Yew logs|Adamantite bar
|Adamantite bar|Adamantite bar|Adamantite bar|Adamantite bar
|Adamantite bar|Adamantite bar|Adamantite bar|Adamantite bar
|Adamantite bar|Adamantite bar|Adamantite bar|Adamantite bar}}
This method requires the [[Fishing cape]] for the teleport to Otto's Grotto, as well as a quick teleport to a bank, such as the Achievement Diary Cape or the [[Enchanted lyre(i)|Enchanted Lyre(i)]]. 

Hastae are unique in that they essentially provide double the experience per bar used, at the expense of using a log in the process. For example, smithing a rune sword requires 1 runite bar, and provides 75 experience, however smithing a rune hasta requires 1 runite bar and 1 magic log, providing 150 experience.

This is useful for players with lots of spare yew logs (for [[adamant hastae]]), magic logs (for [[Rune hasta|rune hastae]]), and who wish to increase their smithing experience/bar without having to go to Giant's Foundry.

===== Process =====
''If using the Achievement diary cape for banking at [[Jarr]], the camera may be oriented to the East for this entire process, making it even lower intensity.''

# Start at a bank, withdraw 13 adamantite/runite bars, and 13 yew/magic logs
# Using the fishing cape, teleport to Otto's grotto; the [[barbarian anvil]] is only one tile away from the teleport
# Smith 13 hastae, return to the bank and repeat.

===Levels 70+: Zalcano===
{{Main|Zalcano}}

Once the player has access to [[Prifddinas]], killing [[Zalcano]] is an excellent way of banking Smithing experience in the form of [[gold ore]], or [[mithril ore]]/[[Mithril bar|bars]] and [[adamantite ore]]/[[Adamantite bar|bars]] in addition of earning ~3,000 Smithing experience per hour while fighting her. The experience rates of the dropped ores/bars will be slower than simply buying gold ore; but the activity is effectively free money-wise, and is much more engaging.

Some recommended activities for the bars obtained from Zalcano:

* [[Giants' Foundry]] for more experience and profit from the bars from the commission rewards.
* Smithed into armour pieces such as [[platebodies]] and casting [[High Level Alchemy|high-level alchemy]] on them for money.
* Turned into [[dart tips]] for the [[toxic blowpipe]].

